-- title:
--   Six separations under the third-period condition
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group. For $a,d,h\in G$ with $2h=0$ and $3d\in\{0,h\}$, the six conditions
--
--   $$a\ne a+d,\quad a\ne a+d+h,\quad a\ne a-d,\quad a\ne a-d+h,\quad a+d\ne a-d,\quad a+d\ne a-d+h$$
--
--   hold if and only if $2d\ne0$. This simplifies the separation test in the third-period case.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourAbelian.lean#L942-L965, lines 942–965; source file SHA-256 c9643d6e3a677d5a903623825d50a309d87175a21ace2b7ab56939d9189f13b1; theorem Couret.CayleyDoublet.abelianThreeSeparations_iff_double_ne_zero

